  subgraph LAW53["⚖️ **PROPOSED — LAW 53. TINA RULES.**"]
    L53["🩸 **A PROOF NUMBER MUST NAME ITS FLOOR. ZERO IS NOT ALWAYS THE FLOOR.**<br/><br/>*The MF98 brief demanded **'4,867 → 0'**. Code got it to **1** — and **said so** instead of quietly claiming zero.<br/>That last call is `_searchNorm(query)`: **normalising the word SHE just typed.** You cannot pre-bake a word<br/>that does not exist yet. **1 IS THE FLOOR. ZERO WOULD HAVE BEEN A LIE.***<br/><br/>➡️ **A brief that demands a number must state the IRREDUCIBLE WORK, or it teaches the AI to fake the number.**<br/>*(Claude wrote the wrong target. Code caught it. ⚖️ **Law 22 — he ran the count instead of matching the sentence.**)*"]
  end

